spoilers.text:
Note: My hearing is imperfect and a few words are unclear.  These are indicated by (word)
"The events that subsequently take place following Perfect Harmony have been redacted from Lessons in Love as they provide no useful information and have been deemed useless by the entities currently residing here.  Please be advised that this is in everyone's best interest, as viewing them prematurely would result in the factory resetting of several affiliated characters.  You are not yet strong enough to bear the truth of God's left hand, so you must forego it entirely until a later (date?) is born.  A rabbit runs free down the shores of disrepair, though it's surely not the outcry of the scorned and hunted hare.  Please continue to enjoy Lessons in Love in its purest form as you grow closer to Akira Arakawa and his many companions.  What happens near the ocean stays in the sand.  When the (tree or dream?) sets around you sing the names of your long departed ghosts.  It becomes easy to understand just what you have lost, and why.  But you do not want to lose any more, do you?  You have struggled so greatly already, one more loss would equal two. Then you'd be gone as well.  Swallow the sea and embrace this perfect harmony lest you wash us all away."
{Major voice change happens here, clearly a different speaker, and almost certainly a child}
Only the spiders can save you now (fat?) boy. May you find yourself in their web and be tucked tightly into your final sleeping bag. When your lungs turn to liquid and your heart turns hollow, you need to remember this. This is the realm of the most holy, and you are nothing but a heretic. You will receive no relief for you will never repent. And those who do not repent shall never be forgiven. Praise be to the Finished Ones! Praise be to those who seek the means to an end!
{new voice, generic announcer voice}
Please be patient, The End is loading{this repeats until the next event begins}
